# My Obsidian - Warp Project Configuration

## Project Overview
My Obsidian is a modern, AI-powered markdown editor that provides full compatibility with Obsidian vaults while adding advanced features like drag-and-drop organization, YouTube video embedding, and semantic search.

## Architecture
- **Frontend**: React + TypeScript + Vite
- **Backend**: FastAPI + Python
- **Database**: SQLite with SQLAlchemy
- **AI**: Google Gemini 2.5 Flash via OpenRouter for chat and semantic search

## Key Features Implemented
✅ YAML Frontmatter Support with dynamic title display
✅ Drag & Drop file organization with folder creation
✅ YouTube video auto-detection and embedding
✅ AI-powered semantic search
✅ Resizable sidebar and split-pane editing
✅ Three view modes: Edit, Preview, Split (Ctrl+E to cycle)
✅ **Synchronized Scrolling in Split View**
✅ Lock/unlock scroll synchronization with button on resize handle
✅ Bidirectional scroll syncing between editor and preview
✅ **Obsidian-style Editor Width Slider**
✅ Status bar with word/character count and width control
✅ Independent width settings for Edit and Preview modes (40-100%)
✅ Beautiful modern UI with gradients and animations
✅ Word wrapping and proper scrolling
✅ Dark/Light theme support
✅ Import Hotspot (Ctrl+Shift+I) for quick URL import and bulk .txt files
✅ YouTube graceful fallback: notes created even without transcripts
✅ Context-aware toasts and badges for YouTube imports
✅ **AI Assistant with Dual Query Modes**
✅ Vault Context Mode: Semantic search across all notes with citations
✅ General Query Mode: Direct AI chat for general knowledge questions
✅ Multi-note querying like NotebookLM (automatic semantic matching)
✅ Non-blocking UI: Continue editing while chatting with AI
✅ Fast responses with Google Gemini 2.5 Flash (~3 seconds)
✅ **Drag & Drop File Upload**
✅ Drag images, JSON, code files, CSV, and markdown directly into editor
✅ Automatic format conversion and insertion at cursor position
✅ Support for 20+ programming languages with syntax highlighting
✅ **NEW: Image Gallery & Management**
✅ View all embedded images across notes in centralized gallery
✅ Delete images in-editor with hover trash or keyboard shortcuts
✅ Full-screen scrollable image viewer
✅ Copy markdown from gallery for quick insertion
✅ **NEW: Advanced UI Customization**
✅ Accent color control with hue and brightness sliders
✅ All toolbar icons dynamically use the accent color
✅ Global text brightness control for entire app
✅ Preview window background color customization (hue + brightness)
✅ Font family and size controls for both editor and preview
✅ Live font preview - see changes instantly in respective windows
✅ 6 file sorting options (name, created, modified - asc/desc)
✅ Folders collapsed by default for cleaner UI
✅ Real-time updates for all settings with instant feedback
✅ All settings persist across sessions via localStorage

## Development Commands

### Frontend
```bash
cd My_Obsidian_FrontEnd-main
npm install
npm run dev        # Development server
npm run build      # Production build
npm run preview    # Preview build
```

### Synchronized Scrolling (Split View)
- **Lock Button** appears on the resize handle between editor and preview panes
- **Click to toggle** scroll synchronization on/off
- **Locked State**: Scrolling in either pane automatically scrolls the other proportionally
- **Unlocked State**: Both panes scroll independently
- **Visual Indicator**: Lock icon (black/white) vs Unlock icon (gray)
- **Smooth Sync**: Maintains relative scroll position across both panes
- **Default**: Locked by default for better UX in split view

### Editor Width Slider
- **Status bar** appears at bottom of editor/preview showing:
  - Word count and character count (left)
  - Width slider with percentage (right)
- **Adjust width** from 40% to 100% in 5% increments
- **Centered content** when width < 100% for focused reading/writing
- **Separate settings** for Edit mode (`editorWidth`) and Preview mode (`previewWidth`)
- **Persistent** settings saved to localStorage
- **Smooth transitions** when adjusting width

### Drag & Drop File Upload
- **Drag files from desktop** directly into the markdown editor
- **Supported file types**:
  - **Images**: JPG, PNG, GIF, WEBP, BMP → Embedded as base64
  - **JSON**: Formatted with syntax highlighting
  - **Code**: Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, Go, Rust, and 15+ more languages
  - **CSV**: Automatically converted to markdown tables
  - **Markdown**: Direct content insertion
- **File size limit**: 10MB per file
- **Visual feedback**: Drag overlay and upload progress indicator
- **Multiple files**: Drop multiple files at once for batch upload
- **Smart insertion**: Files inserted at current cursor position

### Import Hotspot (URLs and Bulk)
- Open via toolbar Import button or Ctrl+Shift+I
- Drag & drop a .txt file containing URLs (one per line)
- Paste a single URL (YouTube, GitHub, article, PDF) for quick import
- Configure AI summary, tags, and target folder
- See real-time progress for bulk imports

### Backend
```bash
cd backend
python runner.py                    # Start both API and file watcher
python -m uvicorn app:app --reload  # API only with auto-reload
python import_notes.py              # Import Obsidian notes
python test_import.py               # Test import with sample
```

### AI Assistant
- **Access**: Click AI Assist button (Sparkles icon) in toolbar
- **Dual Modes**:
  - **Vault Context Mode** (Toggle ON): Searches your notes with semantic similarity, returns answers with citations
  - **General Query Mode** (Toggle OFF): Ask general questions without searching vault
- **Features**:
  - Automatic multi-note querying across entire vault
  - Citations using [[Note Title]] format
  - Conversation history (save/clear options)
  - Configurable settings (model selection, temperature, context size)
  - Non-dimming overlay - continue editing while chatting
- **Models Available**:
  - Google Gemini 2.5 Flash (Default - Fastest)
  - Google Gemini 2.5 Pro
  - GLM-4.6
  - Claude 3.5 Sonnet
  - GPT-4 Turbo/GPT-4
  - Llama 3 70B

### UI Customization (Settings → Appearance)
- **Accent Color**:
  - **Hue Slider**: Pick any color (0-360°) for UI elements
  - **Brightness Slider**: Adjust accent brightness (10-80%, step 6)
  - Affects all toolbar icons, buttons, links, and highlights
  - Changes apply instantly and save automatically
  
- **Text Brightness**:
  - **Luminance Slider**: Control text brightness globally (10-96%, step 6)
  - Affects all text in app (toolbar, sidebar, editor) AND preview window
  - Independent of theme - works in both light and dark modes
  
- **Background Color** (Preview Window):
  - **Hue Slider**: Choose background color tint (0-360°)
  - **Brightness Slider**: Adjust darkness (3-20%) for subtle tinting
  - Only affects preview/reading pane background
  - Works with existing texture and brightness settings
  
- **File Sorting**:
  - Name (A-Z or Z-A)
  - Created Date (Newest First or Oldest First)
  - Modified Date (Newest First or Oldest First)
  - Dropdown in sidebar with real-time sorting
  
- **Folder Behavior**:
  - All folders start collapsed by default
  - Click to expand/collapse individual folders
  - State persists during session
  
- **Font Settings**:
  - **Editor Font**: Family and size (12-20px)
  - **Preview Font**: Family and size (14-22px)
  - **Live Preview**: Changes apply instantly to the respective window
  - **Font Options**: Montserrat, Inter, Georgia, Roboto, JetBrains Mono, Merriweather
  - See exactly how text will look before saving

## Configuration Files
- `backend/config.py` - Vault path and API keys
- `src/lib/api.ts` - Frontend API configuration
- `vite.config.ts` - Build configuration
- `tailwind.config.ts` - Styling configuration

## Port Configuration
- Frontend Dev Server: 5173, 8080, 8081, 8082 (auto-selects)
- Backend API: 8000
- API Documentation: 8000/docs

## Git Workflow
1. Feature branches from main
2. Pull requests for code review
3. Automatic builds on push
4. Production deployments from main

## Dependencies
### Frontend
- React 18.3.1
- TypeScript 5.6
- Vite 5.4
- Tailwind CSS 3.4
- CodeMirror 6
- Shadcn/ui components

### Backend  
- FastAPI (latest)
- SQLAlchemy 2.0
- Python-frontmatter 1.1
- YouTube Transcript API 1.2 + yt-dlp fallback
- OpenRouter API for AI features (Google Gemini, Claude, GPT-4, etc.)

## Environment Setup
1. Node.js 16+ with npm
2. Python 3.8+ with pip
3. Git for version control
4. **Required for AI**: OpenRouter API key in backend/.env as `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`

## Folder Structure
```
My_Obsidian/
├── My_Obsidian_FrontEnd-main/    # React app
│   ├── src/components/AI/        # AI Assistant components
│   │   ├── AIChatPanel.tsx       # Main chat interface
│   │   ├── AISettingsDialog.tsx  # Settings management
│   │   ├── ChatMessage.tsx       # Message display
│   │   └── CitationCard.tsx      # Citation rendering
│   ├── src/components/Editor/    # Editor components
│   │   ├── EnhancedMarkdownEditor.tsx
│   │   ├── MarkdownPreview.tsx
│   │   ├── EditorWidthSlider.tsx
│   │   ├── ScrollLockHandle.tsx
│   │   ├── FileBrowser.tsx
│   │   ├── ImagesGallery.tsx     # Image gallery and management
│   │   └── EditorToolbar.tsx
│   ├── src/lib/                  # Utilities and API
│   └── src/pages/                # Main application
└── backend/                      # FastAPI server
    ├── app.py                    # Main API with AI and file upload endpoints
    ├── database.py               # Models (including AI tables)
    ├── ai.py                     # Embeddings and chat
    ├── ai_service.py             # AI Assistant service layer
    ├── file_processor.py         # File upload processing
    └── import_notes.py           # Import script
```

## Performance Notes
- Frontend bundle: ~1.3MB (compressed: ~427KB)
- Backend startup: <2 seconds
- Note import speed: ~1.1 seconds per note (due to embedding generation)
- Search response time: <100ms for most queries
- **AI Assistant**: ~3 seconds for general queries, ~5-8 seconds for vault context mode (includes semantic search)

## Browser Support
- Chrome/Edge 100+
- Firefox 100+
- Safari 15+
- Mobile browsers supported

## Known Issues
- Large vaults (1000+ notes) may take time to import initially
- YouTube embeds require internet connectivity
- AI features require OpenRouter API key (set in backend/.env)
- YouTube transcripts may be unavailable due to rate limits or video restrictions; notes will still be created with guidance
- Semantic search can be slow on first query as embeddings are generated

## Deployment Notes
- Frontend: Static files, can deploy to Vercel, Netlify, etc.
- Backend: FastAPI server, can deploy to Heroku, Railway, etc.
- Database: SQLite file, consider PostgreSQL for production
- File watcher: Optional for production, mainly for development

## Security Considerations
- API keys stored in environment variables
- CORS configured for development
- Input validation on all endpoints
- SQL injection protection via SQLAlchemy
- File system access limited to configured vault path

## Performance Optimizations
- React Suspense for code splitting
- Vite for fast builds and HMR
- SQLite indexes on frequently queried fields
- Debounced search to reduce API calls
- Lazy loading for large file trees

This project represents a successful integration of modern web technologies with traditional note-taking workflows, providing a powerful and intuitive interface for knowledge management.